  "title": "More capable text requests",
  "summary": "February broadened what people could build with the text API while making requests more private and bringing more community projects into view.\n\nGemini, reasoning, and other model options joined the text API. Function calling and OpenAI-style streaming gave clients more ways to work with responses; follow-up changes tightened stream formatting and errors.\n\nText requests gained a private option, and OpenAI-compatible requests became private by default. Image prompts gained LlamaGuard checks, feed events gained maturity data, and the turbo image model gained prompt enhancement.\n\nNew listings ranged from text adventures and chat apps to coding tools, image generators, bots, a model comparison tool, and Musify. The showcase increasingly reflected what people were already building with the API.\n\nVision and feed documentation became more specific, project submission copy got simpler, and share previews gained a banner that link previews can resolve. Smaller website cleanups removed unused imagery and improved project links.",
